# TW-03 — Prefer theme colors over hardcoded arbitrary colors

## Rationale

Hardcoded arbitrary colors (`bg-[#1a2b3c]`, `text-[rgb(10,10,10)]`) duplicate
brand values in markup and make refactors harder.
Colors that belong to the design system should live in `tailwind.config`.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check tailwind <file>
```

Flags color utilities with arbitrary hex, rgb, hsl, or oklch values.

Before proposing a new color, **read the project's `tailwind.config`** — our
themes usually define a rich palette already.

## Our color patterns

Typical project config includes:

- **Semantic UI tokens**: `foreground`, `background`, `button-text`,
  `button-background`
- **Flat brand/neutral names**: `red`, `pink`, `black`, `dark-gray`,
  `light-gray`, `linen`, `silver`, `yellow`
- **Nested variant objects**: `purple.offwhite`, `purple.DEFAULT`, `purple.dark`

```js
colors: {
  foreground: '#1E1E1E',
  background: '#FFFFFF',
  red: '#F23440',
  'dark-gray': '#4E5357',
  linen: '#FAF1E8',
  purple: {
    offwhite: '#E5DFF2',
    DEFAULT: '#6C5A9F',
    dark: '#58468B',
  },
},
```

Use `text-foreground`, `bg-linen`, `text-purple-dark` — not hex arbitraries.

## How to fix

**Propose** replacing the arbitrary color with an **existing** config token when
one matches (or is close enough).

If no token exists and the color is part of the brand system, add it to config
(see TW-02), then update markup.

**Acceptable** when the color is truly one-off (e.g. a third-party embed) and
should not enter the theme system.

## Examples

### Bad

```html
<p class="text-[#4E5357]">Body copy</p>
<div class="bg-[#FAF1E8] border-[#D4D7D6]">…</div>
<button class="bg-[#6C5A9F]">Shop now</button>
```

### Good — existing theme tokens

```html
<p class="text-dark-gray">Body copy</p>
<div class="bg-linen border-silver">…</div>
<button class="bg-purple">Shop now</button>
```

### Good — semantic UI tokens

```html
<div class="bg-background text-foreground">
  <button class="bg-button-background text-button-text">Add to cart</button>
</div>
```

### Good — add to config when missing

```js
colors: { 'extra-light-gray': '#F4F4F4' },
```

```html
<div class="bg-extra-light-gray">…</div>
```
